00:00:52.240 --> 00:01:01.460
with the S&amp;P 500 finishing at 7,337. That represents a decline of 4 tenths of a percent.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:11.280
The NASDAQ composite closed at 25,806 down 1 tenths of a percent. The TSX composite ended

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:19.900
the session at 33,857, also off 4 tenths of a percent. Caution stems from reminders

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:27.020
of 2019 repo volatility and the risk that balance sheet tightening could still affect liquidity

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:36.160
even if rate cuts proceed. The NASDAQ sits 11.06% higher year-to-date. Our simulated portfolio

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:44.180
shows a cumulative return of 0.01% with a year-to-date move that delivers positive alpha versus

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:51.320
that benchmark. No active quantitative tightening was required for that stress to appear. Some

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:57.260
observers assume the Fed can simply offset slower rate cuts by tweaking balance sheet runoff

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:03.420
at the margin. In practice, the non-linearity of reserved demand and the fragility of money

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:10.200
market plumbing mean those two tools are not clean substitutes. Track weekly reserve levels

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:16.400
and repo rate prints alongside the Fed schedule using data from the New York Fed website or

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:22.080
your broker dashboard. The approach works best historically when reserves approach levels

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:29.660
that stress dealer balance sheets exactly as seen in September 2019. The main risk is

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:34.640
over estimating how quickly the Fed can pivot the balance sheet without creating fresh market

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:41.420
stress. Treat the fund's rate and balance sheet as distinct policy levers rather than interchangeable

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:48.100
knobs. Our practice investment of the day is a simulated weekly hold in snowflake. The ticker

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:55.740
is SNO on the NASDAQ. The strategy is a momentum play on positive intraday price action following

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:02.780
recent data center and cloud demand signals. The hold runs from Monday through Friday. The

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:09.220
catalyst is a nice move in the name amid broader cloud sector interest and upcoming China earning

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:16.180
season that could lift related tech names. On the technical side, price action showed strength relative

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:23.440
to recent session lows. We monitor the 20 day and 50 day moving averages for continuation with

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:31.760
volume confirmation needed above average levels. Risk is managed with a stop loss 6% below entry to

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:38.740
limit drawdown if momentum fades. Position size is capped at 5% of the simulated portfolio.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:45.580
The target is 3 to 6% over the 5 day window if cloud spending data remains supportive.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:54.040
Confidence sits at medium because positive price reaction and sector tailwinds align, yet we lack volume

00:03:54.040 --> 00:04:01.140
or earnings confirmation today. This setup shows how to convert a simple intraday

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:07.380
observation into a structured weekly hold with explicit risk parameters and benchmark comparison.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:14.260
Listeners learn to require at least two confirming factors before committing capital rather than

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:21.800
chasing single day moves. This is a simulated trade for learning purposes only.

