00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:33.900
Now here is something most retail investors get wrong and it cost me money before I figured it out.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:43.180
Imagine you bought a globally diversified ETF like XEQT last week when equity markets dipped on

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:49.540
Fed commentary. Your order filled at the prevailing price but what actually happened between your click

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:56.720
and the execution was a rebalancing flow across stocks, bonds, and international holdings.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:03.240
That flow reduced single asset volatility without lowering expected long-term return.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:10.000
Modern portfolio theory shows that combining assets with low correlations can move your portfolio

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:16.000
closer to the efficient frontier where risk is minimized for any given return target.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:23.120
Strategic allocation sets long-term weights based on your risk tolerance while tactical shifts

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:28.600
respond to short-term signals such as valuation spreads or sector momentum.

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:36.420
Bonds still serve as ballast even after 2022's drawdowns because they provide negative correlation

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:44.540
during equity stress, though the magnitude has varied. Age-based rules like 100-age in stocks

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:51.440
oversimplify because they ignore personal factors such as pension income or TFSA room.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:59.080
Rebalance using threshold triggers, for example, when any asset class drifts more than 5%

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:06.660
from target rather than rigid calendar dates to avoid unnecessary transaction costs inside registered

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:12.640
accounts. The biggest misconception is treating asset allocation as a one-time decision.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:22.560
Instead, review your XBAL or VGRO holdings quarterly against your written risk tolerance statement,

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:29.940
and adjust only when thresholds are breached. Before we wrap, pull up snow's daily chart on your

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:36.820
brokerage platform and mark the 20-day and 50-day moving averages. Note the current distance from

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:44.740
each and set a price alert 2% above the 50-day average. Tomorrow I will examine how next week's China

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:48.840
